midwire-base (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the network link over the USB-C port, which 0.4.0 left "not
    connected" on the computer: the Pi's end was never switched on, because
    the kernel refused the interface name the script asked for. The script
    now asks for a name the kernel accepts and finds the interface by its
    address, not its name.
  * Fix the proxy not being able to start while that link was in this
    state. Bringing the link up now releases the port again if anything
    goes wrong, the proxy's unit releases it directly before starting, and
    switching the link off does too.

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

midwire-base (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * While the proxy is idle, the USB-C port is a USB network adapter (NCM):
    the computer on the other end of the cable gets an address from the Pi
    (10.42.2.1) and can open the web UI. It is a management link only, with
    no gateway and no DNS, so nothing is routed through the Pi. The port is
    handed to usb-proxy when the proxy starts and taken back when it stops.
  * The system helper can switch that link on and off.

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0000

midwire-base (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the system helper behind the web UI's SSH settings: turn SSH on or
    off, set a login user's password (creating the user when the device has
    none) and add or remove that user's SSH keys. Reached over
    /run/midwire/system.sock, which only the web UI's user may open.

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000

midwire-base (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release. Adds the apt source and key for Midwire's packages, the
    updater behind the web UI's Updates page with a daily check, and the
    udev rule that keeps NetworkManager off network interfaces on USB
    devices (moved here from the image so existing devices get it).

 -- Sidhant Goel <sidhant@hexcod.in>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
